23. Patient File is a physical and systemic object.
24. Patient Information is an informatical and systemic object.
25. Patient List is an informatical and systemic object.
26. Print is a physical and systemic object.
27. Registration Form is a physical and systemic object.
28. Registration Form can be handed in, recorded or stored.
29. State recorded is initial.
30. Tape is a physical and systemic object.
31. Treatment Plan is an informatical and systemic object.
32. Patient Intake Handling is a physical and systemic process.
33. Family Doctor, First Intaker, Nursing Officer, Psychiatrist, Second Intaker, Secretarial Office, and Team Leader handle Patient Intake Handling.
34. Patient Intake Handling requires Dictaphone, Medical File Copy, Personal Notebook, and Telephone.
35. Patient Intake Handling affects Information System, Medical File, New Notice List, Patient, Registration Card, and Standard Checklist.
36. Patient Intake Handling yields Assignment List, Letter, Meeting, Notice, Patient File, Patient Information, Patient List, Print, Registration Form, Tape, and Treatment Plan.
# SD1
1. Patient Intake Handling from SD zooms in SD1 into Notice Giving, Patient Inquiring, Doctor Connecting, Patient State Inquiring, Registration Form Handing, Information Storing, Information Printing, Patient File Creating, Registration Form Storing, Registration Card Producing, Patient Listing, Intaker Assigning, Medical File Determining, Assignment Storing, Registration Card Passing, Letter Sending, Second Intaker Informing, Copy Adding, First Meeting Planning, Patient Examining, Observation Registering, Notes Filing, Second Meeting Planning, Observation Recording, Tape Typing, Patient List Providing, and Treatment Plan Formulating, which occur in that time sequence.
