40. Patient Intake Handling is a physical and systemic process.
41. Notice Giving is an informatical and environmental process.
42. Family Doctor handles Notice Giving.
43. Notice Giving requires Telephone.
44. Notice Giving yields Notice.
45. Patient Inquiring is an informatical and systemic process.
46. Secretarial Office handles Patient Inquiring.
47. Patient Inquiring requires Notice.
48. Patient Inquiring yields Patient Information.
49. Doctor Connecting is an informatical and systemic process.
50. Secretarial Office handles Doctor Connecting.
51. Doctor Connecting requires Patient Information.
52. Doctor Connecting affects Notice.
53. Patient State Inquiring is a physical and systemic process.
54. Family Doctor and Nursing Officer handle Patient State Inquiring.
55. Patient State Inquiring yields Registration Form.
56. Registration Form Handing is a physical and systemic process.
57. Registration Form Handing changes Registration Form from recorded to handed in.
58. Nursing Officer handles Registration Form Handing.
59. Information Storing is an informatical and systemic process.
60. Secretarial Office handles Information Storing.
61. Information Storing requires Registration Form at state handed in.
62. Information Storing affects Information System.
63. Information Printing is a physical and systemic process.
64. Secretarial Office handles Information Printing.
65. Information Printing requires Information System.
66. Information Printing yields Print.
67. Patient File Creating is a physical and systemic process.
68. Secretarial Office handles Patient File Creating.
69. Patient File Creating yields Patient File.
70. Registration Form Storing is a physical and systemic process.
71. Registration Form Storing changes Registration Form from handed in to stored.
72. Secretarial Office handles Registration Form Storing.
73. Registration Form Storing affects Patient File.
74. Registration Card Producing is a physical and systemic process.
75. Secretarial Office handles Registration Card Producing.
76. Registration Card Producing yields Registration Card.
77. Patient Listing is an informatical and systemic process.
78. Secretarial Office handles Patient Listing.
79. Patient Listing affects New Notice List.
80. Intaker Assigning is an informatical and systemic process.
81. Team Leader handles Intaker Assigning.
82. Intaker Assigning requires New Notice List.
83. Intaker Assigning yields Assignment List.
84. Medical File Determining is an informatical and systemic process.
85. Team Leader handles Medical File Determining.
86. Medical File Determining affects Assignment List and Medical File.
87. Assignment Storing is an informatical and systemic process.
88. Secretarial Office handles Assignment Storing.
89. Assignment Storing requires Assignment List.
90. Assignment Storing affects Information System.
91. Registration Card Passing is a physical and systemic process.
92. Secretarial Office handles Registration Card Passing.
93. Registration Card Passing affects Registration Card.
94. Letter Sending is a physical and systemic process.
95. Secretarial Office handles Letter Sending.
96. Letter Sending occurs if Medical File is at state required, otherwise Letter Sending is skipped.
97. Letter Sending yields Letter.
98. Second Intaker Informing is an informatical and systemic process.
99. Secretarial Office handles Second Intaker Informing.
100. Medical File Copy initiates Second Intaker Informing, which requires Medical File Copy.
101. Second Intaker Informing affects Second Intaker.
102. Copy Adding is a physical and systemic process.
103. Secretarial Office handles Copy Adding.
104. Copy Adding requires Medical File Copy.
105. Copy Adding affects Patient File.
106. First Meeting Planning is an informatical and systemic process.
107. First Intaker handles First Meeting Planning.
108. First Meeting Planning yields Meeting.
109. Patient Examining is a physical and systemic process.
110. First Intaker handles Patient Examining.
111. Patient Examining requires Meeting.
112. Patient Examining affects Patient and Standard Checklist.
113. Observation Registering is a physical and systemic process.
114. First Intaker handles Observation Registering.
115. Observation Registering affects Personal Notebook.
116. Notes Filing is a physical and systemic process.
117. First Intaker handles Notes Filing.
118. Notes Filing requires Personal Notebook and Standard Checklist.
119. Notes Filing affects Patient File.
120. Second Meeting Planning is an informatical and systemic process.
121. Second Intaker handles Second Meeting Planning.
122. Second Meeting Planning yields Meeting.
123. Observation Recording is a physical and systemic process.
124. Second Intaker handles Observation Recording.
125. Observation Recording requires Dictaphone.
126. Observation Recording yields Tape.
127. Tape Typing is a physical and systemic process.
128. Secretarial Office handles Tape Typing.
129. Tape Typing requires Tape.
130. Tape Typing affects Patient File.
131. Patient List Providing is an informatical and systemic process.
132. Secretarial Office handles Patient List Providing.
133. Patient List Providing yields Patient List.
134. Treatment Plan Formulating is an informatical and systemic process.
135. First Intaker, Psychiatrist, Second Intaker, and Team Leader handle Treatment Plan Formulating.
136. Treatment Plan Formulating requires Patient List.
137. Treatment Plan Formulating yields Treatment Plan.
